@startuml
title Topology-first region solve (proposed replacement for SeedPlacer/RegionSolver's flood-fill-first flow)

start
:Chunk request lands in an unsolved region;
:Check all 4 neighbor directions for an already-cached region\n(never force-solve one that's missing - ARCHITECTURE.md invariant);
:Fix those cached edges' macro-cell biome-ids as boundary context;
:Reset dropped-node count = 0;

repeat
  :Build abstract seed graph for region\n(see seed-graph-generation.puml);

  if (graph connectivity sane\n(not flagged for reseed)?) then (yes)
    :Run CSP identity assignment on abstract graph\n(see csp-identity-assignment.puml);
  else (no)
  endif

  if (assignment found?) then (yes)
  else (no)
    if (reseed attempts remaining\nat this dropped-node count?) then (yes)
      :Discard graph, regenerate seed scatter\n(cheap - abstract graph only, no geometry to undo);
    else (no)
      if (more than 1 interior node\nstill remains in the graph?) then (yes)
        :Drop the most-constrained interior node\nentirely (its territory absorbs into\nneighbors at geometry time - safe,\nnothing geometric committed yet);
        :Increment dropped-node count,\nreset reseed budget;
      else (no)
        :FAIL LOUD - crash with diagnostic\n(fixed boundary context already\ncontains an illegal edge - the only\ncase this ladder cannot resolve);
        stop
      endif
    endif
  endif
repeat while (assignment not found) is (retry)
->resolved;

:Realize geometry onto macro-cell grid\nfrom fixed topology + identities\n(see geometry-realization.puml);

if (any cell stranded, or patch short of its min size?) then (yes)
  :Local repair: adjust weights or\nmerge/reshuffle a small neighborhood only\n(not a full region re-solve);
else (no)
endif

:Write macro-cell -> biome-id for region to cache;
stop

note right
  Every fallback tier only REMOVES or REGENERATES
  graph structure - reseed (new scatter) and node-drop
  (territory absorbed by neighbors pre-geometry) - it
  never commits an edge the compatibility graph forbids.

  Node-drop is NOT capped at a small arbitrary constant
  like GapFiller's pixel-level MAX_PATCH_DROP_RETRIES (3,
  tuned empirically because dropping pixel patches is
  expensive and testing showed raising it just relocated
  crashes further into the region, not eliminated them -
  see KNOWN_ISSUES.md). Dropping a node only ever REMOVES
  a constraint, never adds one, so it's monotonic: floor
  out at 1 interior node, and that node is provably
  colorable (zero remaining edges to violate, and its
  domain is non-empty by construction - BiomeGraph
  guarantees at least one identity exists with no
  incompatible-neighbor constraint on an unconstrained
  node). This is a PROOF of eventual success, not a tuned
  cap, because the graph is dozens of nodes (cheap to
  drop down to 1) - the same guarantee pixel-level
  GapFiller can't afford at thousands-of-cells scale.

  FAIL LOUD is reachable in exactly one case: the fixed
  boundary itself already contains an illegal edge
  (inherited from a buggy neighbor-region cache) - nothing
  this region's own ladder does can un-fix a contradiction
  baked into input it doesn't control. That's a genuine
  invariant violation elsewhere, correctly loud here. See
  feedback_fail_loud memory: prove the bad state
  unreachable by construction; this ladder does that for
  every case except an already-corrupt boundary.
end note
@enduml
